## 🔄 Database Replication

Based on master/slave model:

```
        Writes
Client ──────→ Master DB
                  │
         Replication (async)
        ┌─────────┼─────────┐
        ▼         ▼         ▼
     Slave 1   Slave 2   Slave 3
     (reads)   (reads)   (reads)
```

**Advantages:**
| Benefit | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| **Performance** | Writes on master, reads distributed across slaves |
| **Reliability** | Data preserved even if one server destroyed |
| **High Availability** | Website stays up even if a DB goes offline |

**Failure Scenarios:**
- **One slave offline** → reads redirected to master or other slaves temporarily
- **Master offline** → a slave is promoted to master (may need data recovery scripts)

