## 🌐 Content Delivery Network (CDN)

A geographically dispersed network of servers for delivering **static content** (JS, CSS, images, videos).

```
User (Los Angeles) → CDN Edge Server (LA) → Static Asset
                                ↓ (cache miss)
                         Origin Server (S3/Web Server)
```

**CDN Workflow:**
1. User requests `image.png` via CDN URL
2. CDN checks cache → if miss, fetches from origin
3. Origin returns file with optional TTL header
4. CDN caches & returns to user; subsequent users get cached version

**CDN Considerations:**

| Factor | Detail |
|--------|--------|
| **Cost** | Charged per data transfer; only cache frequently used assets |
| **Cache Expiry** | Balance freshness vs. load (not too long, not too short) |
| **CDN Fallback** | App must handle CDN outage gracefully |
| **File Invalidation** | Use CDN API or URL versioning (`image.png?v=2`) |

